{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:a8e96011b04e0940","name":"Old Republic Captain","source":{"id":"source:reference-a8e96011b04e0940","title":"Old Republic Captain","revision":19273,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:38:27Z","sha256":"9de66429233ddd6b376ab8488637d45d85f10a3691113b2c5705817f2c37c79a","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19273","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Old%20Republic%20Captain&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-a8e96011b04e0940","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic","referenceId":"reference:6517b7e15507b001"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Republic Navy's training system is directed toward a single goal: generating quality captains to helm vessels. In the earlier days of the smaller Navy, this took on added importance, as commands were few and ships were precious. Competition remains cutthroat into the early years of the Restoration, but the burgeoning number of available postings turns what was once a privilege into an expectation. The majority of spacefaring captains receive a cruiser of some kind to command.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["As such, the pool of Old Republic Captains is somewhat weaker at the onset of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Mandalorian Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Mandalorian_Wars"},", and opportunities for captains to distinguish themselves are excellent. Occasionally, a Captain with special experience is tapped to helm a larger vessel normally reserved for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Old Republic Admirals"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Old_Republic_Admirals"},"; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Saul Karath"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Saul_Karath","referenceId":"reference:71c4ad7788fc4d79"},", present at field tests of the Vanjervalis data systems, received ",{"tag":"i","children":["Courageous"]}," while still waiting for his Merit Board to meet on his promotion to rear admiral. The glut of captains also makes the admiralty less reluctant to allow captains to join their surface teams in action. Captains are not exactly expendable, but they are readily replaceable.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Pay for captains is based on the size of ship they command, with cruiser captains receiving nearly twice what the handful of frigate captains earn. The few captains serving as Space Station administrators earn the least.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Old Republic Captain Statistics (CL 10)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 4/",{"tag":"a","children":["Noble"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble","referenceId":"reference:190d375ec3483f8f"}," 5/",{"tag":"a","children":["Officer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Officer","referenceId":"reference:192135a8adabe174"}," 4\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +12; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +12\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, Bocce, Dur